  "usage": {
    "status": "verified",
    "verifiedAt": "2026-06-08",
    "resultPull": "poll",
    "auth": "siwx",
    "callShape": "POST https://stablesocial.dev/api/tiktok/following with JSON body {handle, max_page_size?, order_by?, cursor?} (x402-paid ~$0.06). Returns HTTP 202 async job. Then GET the returned pollUrl with SIWX auth from the SAME wallet that paid until body.status===\"finished\".",
    "inputExample": {
      "handle": "tiktok",
      "max_results": 1
    },
    "outputShape": "POST -> body.jobId, body.pollUrl, body.token, body.status (pending). Poll (GET pollUrl, SIWX) -> body.status (pending|finished), final following profiles at body.data.items[] (each item: id, username, full_name, avatar_url, follower_count, following_count, heart_count, video_count, is_verified, is_private).",
    "quirks": [
      "The required field is 'handle' (the TikTok username), NOT 'profile_id' — sending profile_id returns HTTP 400 'Validation failed: expected string at path handle'.",
      "POST returns HTTP 202 with an async job (jobId+pollUrl+token, status=pending) — the following list is NOT in the POST response.",
      "The pollUrl REQUIRES SIWX wallet auth from the SAME wallet that paid for the job; an unauthenticated GET returns 402 'SIWX authentication required'.",
      "Poll with SIWX (e.g. qa-pay --siwx GET pollUrl) — polling is free (no extra charge). Loop until body.status==='finished'; provider is data365 and the job took ~50s (8 polls at 6-8s) in this test.",
      "Result data lives at body.data.items[] on the finished poll response, not in the POST body. Some items have null engagement fields (private/uncrawlable profiles).",
      "Server normalizes input to {handle, max_page_size:100} internally; max_results in the body was accepted but the effective cap shows as max_page_size:100."
    ],
    "needs": [],
    "needsApproval": false,
    "guide": "POST to https://stablesocial.dev/api/tiktok/following with JSON {\"handle\":\"<tiktok username>\",\"max_page_size\":N}; this is x402-paid (~$0.06) and returns a 202 async job with jobId, pollUrl, token, status:pending. Then GET the returned pollUrl using SIWX authentication signed by the SAME wallet that paid (an unauthenticated poll fails with 'SIWX authentication required'); polling is free. Repeat the poll every ~5s until body.status === \"finished\", then read the followed accounts from body.data.items[] (each has id, username, full_name, follower_count, following_count, heart_count, video_count, is_verified). Note the field is 'handle', not 'profile_id'.",
    "costObservedUsd": 0.06
  },
  "droppedReason": null,
